# Every documentation script and i18n test in this repo reads its files byte-wise and
# splits on "\n": `normalize-doc-headers.mjs`, `normalize-doc-links.mjs` and
# `gen-docs.mjs --check` all compare a rewrite against the bytes on disk. With git's
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the default of the Git for Windows build bundled here) a fresh
# checkout hands those files CRLF endings, the comparison sees a difference on every
# line, and `npm run check` reports "header is not canonical in N file(s)" even though
# the committed content is correct.
#
# Forcing LF in the worktree keeps the checkout byte-identical to the blobs, so the
# checks measure the docs rather than the checkout. There are no `.cmd`/`.bat` files
# here that would need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
